# Settings for the rangerly-wt / rangerly-pr workflow, for the Rangerly
# MARKETING ASSET library.
#
# The scripts live in ~/Work/Personal/dotfiles (bin/rangerly-*, lib/).
# Precedence: environment variable > this file > the script's own default.
#
# This repo is asset folders, not an application: there is nothing to build and
# nothing to serve. It is here for the branch/worktree/card/PR half of the
# workflow only.
#
# Everything that drives a dev server is deliberately empty, and each empty
# value switches a step off rather than failing it:
#
#   PROJECT       no project directory
#   WATCH_CMD     no server, so rangerly-wt creates a two-pane tab (claude +
#                 shell) and rangerly-run/rangerly-open decline politely
#   DOMAIN_SUFFIX no Caddy route and no hostname
#   PORT_MIN/MAX  no port is allocated, so none is consumed
#   FUNC_PROJECT  no Functions host

PROJECT=""
RUN_DIR=.
WATCH_CMD=""
RUN_CMD=""
RUN_ENV=""
DOMAIN_SUFFIX=""
PORT_MIN=""
PORT_MAX=""
FUNC_PROJECT=""

# The herdr workspace these tabs are grouped into.
WORKSPACE_LABEL="Rangerly Marketing"

# This repo has no integration branch; main is the only one.
BASE_BRANCH=main

# Fizzy columns, matched by name against the card's own board. The
# "Rangerly - Marketing" board has only the built-in Not Now / Maybe? / Done
# columns, so there is no "Active Work" or "Awaiting QA" to move a card into.
# Empty means "leave the card where it is" -- cards still get their comments.
# Add the columns to the board and fill these in to turn the moves on.
ACTIVE_COLUMN=""
QA_COLUMN=""
